 Why: `d` is a `Res` that is still open here, and its `defer close` runs when its scope ends, after this call returns; the call keeps its frame, so a chain of such calls grows the stack
 Fix: Close `d` before the call with `close(^d)` (bind any argument that reads it first), or open it in a smaller block that ends before the call
More: jet-lang.dev/e/L0533

